       "insert": "# How much of the temperature–ozone effect is real?\n\n`datasets::airquality`, 153 rows. Ozone is missing in 37 rows and Solar.R in 7, so\n111 rows have every variable. All numbers below come from run\n`airquality-temp-5` (`analysis.R`, digest `1f6dd06c…`) and from\n`artifact.check` on that run, which reported `integrity: verified` for four files.\n\n## Models\n\n| model | specification | n | temp effect (ppb/°F) | 95% CI | share of A |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A | Ozone ~ Temp | 116 | 2.429 | 1.967 – 2.891 | 1.000 |\n| B | Ozone ~ Temp + Wind | 116 | 1.840 | 1.345 – 2.335 | 0.758 |\n| C | Ozone ~ Temp + Wind, complete rows only | 111 | 1.828 | 1.331 – 2.324 | 0.752 |\n| D | Ozone ~ Temp + Wind + Solar.R | 111 | 1.652 | 1.150 – 2.155 | 0.680 |\n\n## Decomposition of the 32% drop\n\n- **Wind adjustment: −24.2 points** (A → B). This is the real confounder:\n  adding one variable removes a quarter of the raw temperature effect, and the\n  nested F test says the added term earns its place (F = 21.2, p = 1.1e−05).\n- **Sample restriction: −0.5 points** (B → C). Dropping the five rows that lack\n  Solar.R changes almost nothing, so the missingness is not driving the story.\n- **Solar radiation: −7.2 points** (C → D). Smaller, but not noise: F = 6.66,\n  p = 0.011.\n\nSo the honest sentence is: **temperature still matters after adjustment — about\ntwo-thirds of the raw slope survives — but a third of the raw slope was wind and\nsunlight, and wind is by far the larger share.** The raw 2.43 ppb/°F figure is not\na causal effect of temperature.\n\n## What this run does not say\n\n- No causality, no time structure: these are daily measurements with a strong\n  seasonal correlation between temperature and solar radiation.\n- The 37 missing ozone rows are assumed missing at random; nothing here tests that.\n- One dataset, one specification family. Ozone ~ Temp + Wind + Solar.R + Month\n  would be the next thing to try.\n"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "receipts": [
    {
     "kind": "edit",
     "version": 2,
     "at": "2026-10-24T14:48:32.122Z",
